  "text_input": "A 72-year-old female presented with altered sensorium, headache, and difficulty in speech for one day. She is a known case of Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus for 30 years, dyslipidemia, and newly detected hypertension. Clinical examination revealed tachycardia (pulse 120 bpm) and a confusional state. Laboratory investigations showed an HbA1c of 10.3% (EAG 251 mg/dL) and microcytic hypochromic anemia. Liver function tests were normal (Bilirubin 0.3 mg/dL, Albumin 3.8 g/dL). Imaging revealed grade 1 fatty liver and cholelithiasis. Echocardiography showed concentric LVH, diastolic dysfunction, and a normal ejection fraction of 58%. The patient was managed with insulin (Actrapid, Lantus), antibiotics (Cefasultum), and antihypertensives (Cilacar).",
